    "caption": "🤨 One AI model averages 7 em dashes per answer. Claude Opus uses almost none\n\nArtificial Analysis counted every em dash in every answer on its personality benchmark. Plenty of readers treat that dash as a sign a text was written by AI.\n\nThe heaviest user is GLM-5.3, from China's Z.ai, with 7.4 per response. Right behind: GLM-5.3-Flash and Meta's Muse Wonder (6.9 each), then Kimi K3 (6.7).\n\nAnthropic's models are split. Claude Fable 5.1 averages 6.4 per answer. Claude Opus 5.5 uses fewer than one every 40 answers, and Sonnet 5.5 and Haiku 5.5 come out at zero.\n\nSo does OpenAI's old GPT-3.5 Turbo.\n\n@aipost 🏴",
