    "caption": "🤖 A Chinese lab just let anyone download an AI that keeps up with Claude and GPT\n\nMoonshot AI posted the full weights of Kimi K3.1 Pro on Hugging Face. Anyone can now run the model on their own hardware.\n\nIt's enormous: 2.8 trillion parameters, with 104 billion active at a time, and it can read up to 1 million tokens at once.\n\nOn Moonshot's own tests it beats Claude Opus 5.5, Claude Fable 5.1 and GPT-6 Astra on the SWE Marathon coding benchmark: 51.7 against 46.3, 45.6 and 42.5. On Humanity's Last Exam with tools it scores 70.0, ahead of Opus at 67.7.\n\nIt still trails them elsewhere. On ExploitBench, a hacking test, Kimi gets 74.7. GPT-6 Astra gets 100.\n\n@aipost 🏴",
